{
  "name": "Monitor new token listings from 10 crypto exchanges and send alerts to Telegram",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Crypto exchange listing alerts, no account needed\n\nWatches 10 crypto exchanges and posts every new token listing to Telegram, with optional Discord and Google Sheets copies.\n\n### How it works\n\n1. **Every 5 minutes** starts the run.\n2. **Your settings** holds everything you might want to change: which exchanges, spot or futures, a keyword filter, how far back to look, and whether to also send to Discord or log to a sheet.\n3. **Fetch new listings** calls a free, public, read-only JSON feed. No account, no API key, no token.\n4. **Feed returned items?** guards the rest of the run, so an empty or failed response ends quietly instead of throwing.\n5. **Only listings not seen before** remembers each listing's permalink across executions, so a restart or an overlapping window never re-announces one.\n6. Two filters narrow the stream to the exchanges and keywords you care about.\n7. **Prepare alert fields** picks the headline in your language and builds the message.\n8. Spot and futures listings take separate Telegram branches so each reads differently.\n\n### Setup\n\n1. Add a **Telegram** credential, using a bot token from @BotFather.\n2. Open **Your settings** and set `telegram_chat_id` to your chat, group or channel ID.\n3. Leave `send_to_discord` and `log_to_sheet` as `false` unless you want them. To use them, paste a Discord webhook URL, or pick a Google Sheets credential and set the spreadsheet ID.\n4. Save, then activate the workflow.\n\n### Customization tips\n\nNarrow the feed with `exchanges` (`binance,okx`) or `listing_type` (`spot` or `futures`). Raise `lookback_days` up to 30 to backfill on the first run. Titles arrive in three languages, so `title.en`, `title.zh` and `title.ko` are all available.",
        "height": 380,
        "width": 620,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1. Poll the public feed\nA schedule trigger, your settings in one place, one HTTP request to a free read-only endpoint, and a guard so an empty response ends the run quietly. No credential is needed here.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 800,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        400
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2. One item per listing, new ones only\nSplit Out expands the array. Remove Duplicates stores every permalink already handled. The two filters keep only the exchanges and keywords you chose in settings.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 880,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        760,
        400
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3. Build the message\nPick the headline in your language, join the token symbols, work out how old the announcement is, and compose the text once for every channel.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 200,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004",
      "name": "Sticky Note3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1660,
        400
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 4. Deliver\nSpot and futures get separate Telegram branches so each reads differently. Discord and Google Sheets are optional and stay off until you switch them on in settings.",
        "height": 680,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005",
      "name": "Sticky Note4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1880,
        160
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "minutes",
              "minutesInterval": 5
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006",
      "name": "Every 5 minutes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        0,
        480
      ],
      "notes": "How often to check the feed. Every 5 minutes is a good balance; the feed is cached for 5 minutes anyway."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "manual",
        "includeOtherFields": true,
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
